  repository imports the library but does not contain or redistribute it.
- scikit-learn (BSD-3-Clause), pandas (BSD-3-Clause), numpy (BSD-3-Clause),
  joblib (BSD-3-Clause): model training / inference dependencies.

Data redistributed in this repository
-------------------------------------
- codon_usage_freq_table_human.csv — human codon usage frequencies,
  derived from the Kazusa Codon Usage Database (Homo sapiens). The file
  was originally obtained via the LinearDesign distribution
  (Nature 2023); Kazusa codon usage data is freely usable with
  attribution.
- models/composite_v2_stats.pkl — codon-pair statistics built from human
  CDS extracted from Ensembl GRCh38 (freely redistributable data).
- models/oracle_v0_*.joblib, models/utr_m1psi_gbdt.joblib — model weights
  trained in this project on the public data listed below.

Data used for training / validation (NOT redistributed; fetch scripts in
scripts/fetch_upstream_data.sh)
---------------------------------
- Wu et al. 2019, eLife (CC-BY 4.0), fig1-data2 — per-codon optimization
  coefficients (293T/HeLa/RPE/ORFome/K562 experiments).
- PaxDB — integrated protein abundance (CC-BY-SA 4.0).
- Ensembl GRCh38 — CDS/peptide sequences (freely redistributable).
- Bazzini et al. 2016, Science SI — poly(A)-tail / translation data.
- Sample et al. 2019, Nature Biotechnology, GEO GSE114002 — MPRA
  5'UTR expression data (m1psi / unmod conditions).
- GEMORNA, Science 2025, supplementary data S1-S4 — external
  wet-lab validation set and benchmark baseline.

